  "selection_rule": "Preregistered before any reader or oracle ran on these subjects. Public repositories, each at the pinned commit. A root is a directory that directly holds .tf files and passes all of: (1) at least one managed resource block; (2) every resource and data block type, and every provider block, belongs to a provider in providers (the type prefix before the first underscore, aws_s3_bucket is aws); (3) every module block has a local source (starting ./ or ../), because the oracle is run offline after the pinned provider mirror; (4) every required_providers entry names a provider in providers, from the hashicorp namespace; (5) the directory holds no .tofu, .tf.json or override file; (6) it is not under a wrappers directory. Candidates are ordered by sha256(repo + '/' + path) and the first per_repo_cap are kept. The rule reads file text and paths only. The oracle may later reject a selected root (init or show fails offline) and the reading counts each rejection by root.",
